  "description": "QEBNAP crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H100 Cl2 N8 O18 Yb4 2+,2(C1 H2 Cl2),2(H2 O1),2(F6 P1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.435-3.814 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.65-111.11°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Yb4(L)4(H2O)2Cl2](PF6)2·2CH2Cl2·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
